- Add: sliding-window (partitioned) refresh support for MongoDB FDAs, for both `filter` and `aggregation` queries, mirroring the existing PostgreSQL window refresh policy (#194)
- Fix: FDA upload flow now marks status as `completed` only after `defaultDataAccess` is created (308)
- Replace MinIO docker image by PGsty image (#302)
- Fix: MongoDB FDA aggregation pipelines are now validated against an allowlist of read-only stages instead of a blacklist of write stages. Cross-collection stages (`$lookup`, `$graphLookup`, `$unionWith`, `$documents`) and administrative/introspection stages (e.g. `$indexStats`, `$currentOp`) are no longer permitted, including when nested inside a `$facet` sub-pipeline. Existing FDAs using a now-disallowed stage will fail on their next refresh/query execution (#286)
